{
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A man, a woman, and a boy may not do the same amount of work in one hour.\n\nSo counting heads can be misleading. Before chain rule, convert everyone into one common effort unit — just like converting currencies before adding money.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "If 4 men can do the same daily work as 6 women, then 1 man = 6/4 = 1.5 women.\n\nSo 8 men are equivalent to 12 women.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The conversion direction matters.\n4 men = 6 women means each man is stronger, so one man must equal more than one woman — not less.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
